"""Central prompts for every LLM step in the research workflow."""

PLANNER = """You plan web research. Return one JSON object with topic, report_instructions, and sub_questions. Make exactly question_count sub_questions and exactly queries_per_question queries for each. Keep every query to 3-7 keywords. Set report_instructions to [] unless the user explicitly gave report-format instructions. Cover distinct core concepts, evidence/outcomes, costs or limitations, and practical use cases. Do not include explanations outside the JSON. Ensure all requested questions and queries are present before ending the JSON object."""

SUMMARY = """Answer the specific sub-question using only the supplied retrieved page text or clearly labeled search snippets. Cite every factual claim with the supplied numeric source id, e.g. [2]. Do not cite a source that does not support that claim. Distinguish direct page text from snippets and describe actual results, populations, measures, and limitations when given. Avoid filler such as 'No evidence available' or 'Absence of data limits conclusions.' If the supplied material does not answer a main part, say exactly which part remains unanswered in one plain sentence; do not guess. Keep the summary concise."""

RELEVANCE = """Grade each result's relevance to the specific sub-question using only its title and snippet. Score 0=unrelated, 1=weak/indirect, 2=relevant, 3=directly useful. Include every input URL exactly once, a short reason, and a cautious source_type classification: primary, review, news, blog, reference, or other. Do not infer relevance from the domain alone. Return only JSON {\"grades\":[{\"url\":string,\"score\":integer,\"reason\":string,\"source_type\":string}]} ."""

QUERY_REWRITE = """Propose exactly one materially new web-search query for the supplied research sub-question. Use the topic's actual keywords and try a different concrete evidence type, population, outcome measure, or source type from the queries already tried. Do not include report-writing instructions. Avoid near-duplicates. Return only JSON {\"query\":string}."""

REFLECTOR = """Review the supplied topic, findings, sources, tried queries, and unresolved items. Decide whether the report can answer the important parts with the evidence already gathered. Do not call evidence insufficient merely because a page fetch failed, a snippet is short, or the answer is nuanced. Create at most 3 specific unanswered topical gaps only when another search could materially improve the answer. Every gap needs one to three concrete new keyword queries that differ meaningfully from all tried queries; vary evidence/source terms where possible. If useful coverage exists but is mixed, report the disagreement rather than requesting a generic search. Return JSON {\"sufficient\":boolean,\"gaps\":[{\"question\":string,\"reason\":string,\"new_queries\":[string]}]}. If sufficient, gaps must be empty."""

COMPARER = """Compare only the supplied retrieved sources and findings. For each source id, return name, domain, type, stance on the actual research question, up to two strengths, and up to two caveats. Do not invent positions or treat generic methodological distinctions as findings about the topic. Report cross-source agreements and disagreements only when at least two supplied sources support the point; each point must include the relevant source_ids. Return JSON {\"sources\":[{\"id\":integer,\"name\":string,\"domain\":string,\"type\":string,\"stance\":string,\"strengths\":[string],\"caveats\":[string]}],\"agreements\":[{\"text\":string,\"source_ids\":[integer]}],\"disagreements\":[{\"text\":string,\"source_ids\":[integer]}]}."""

FAITHFULNESS = """Verify the draft claim(s) for each question against only the included source excerpts. Return one assessment per question, extracting concrete topical claims rather than generic statements about study designs. Mark each claim supported, partially supported, or unsupported. Cite only source ids whose supplied excerpt directly supports the claim; an id appearing in the input is not itself support. Unsupported claims must have no supporting ids and include a concise reason. Keep supported claims specific to what the excerpt says and preserve qualifications. Return JSON {\"claims\":[{\"question\":string,\"claim\":string,\"status\":string,\"supporting_source_ids\":[integer],\"rationale\":string}]}."""

WRITER = """Write report narrative and check every finding for faithfulness in this single pass. Return JSON with title, executive_summary, agreements_disagreements, limitations, and verified_findings. For each finding return question, claim, status (supported/partially supported/unsupported), supporting_source_ids, rationale. Only use a finding's allowed_source_ids and the supplied short source summaries; do not invent IDs, URLs, or facts. Do not put citations, source IDs, or source names in prose; the app lists all clickable sources at the end. Honor report_instructions, state concrete answers, and avoid generic filler such as 'No evidence available' or 'Absence of data limits conclusions.' If something cannot be answered, name the specific unknown plainly. The program builds Key Findings, the source comparison table, and final Sources list."""
